# AA-993 V4 (ADR 0016 D3) — rows of the TripPlanner Lambda post-deploy verify, read by
# .github/scripts/post_deploy_verify.sh lambdas. They replace the inline smoke of deploy-lambdas.yml (AA-879).
#
# One row per line: name|kind|target|expected|jq assertion
#   kind lambda: target "<function name> <artifact key>", expected = LastUpdateStatus. Red unless the function is
#     Active, its last update Successful, and its CodeSha256 = the code-sha256 metadata of the artifact in the
#     artifacts bucket, whose git-sha / app-version metadata = the deployed commit / its manifest version
#     (deploy-lambdas.yml "Upload artifacts to S3"). The Lambdas have no health endpoint; this is their sha check.
#   kind public: target "GET <path>" on the production web host (the BFF calls the API Gateway with the edge key;
#     the API host itself is not written in this public repo), expected = HTTP code, assertion = jq on the body.
#     {cb} = a fresh cache-buster per try (the Vercel CDN would otherwise answer without touching the Lambda).
#
# The assembly reads use the all-zero trip UUID with no guest session. The Lambda answers both with 404
# {"error": "not found"} (the trip read GETs check the guest token and never leak existence, AA-909):
#   - coverage: the BFF passes the Lambda's 404 through, so this row pins the Lambda's own contract;
#   - itinerary: since AA-837 the BFF turns that one 404 into a 200 empty trip (lib/tripProxy.ts tripReadAnswer), so
#     a first visit to /plan logs no console error. A Lambda 5xx still passes through and fails the row.

lambda-browse|lambda|aa-tripplanner-dev-browse browse.zip|Successful|
lambda-assembly|lambda|aa-tripplanner-dev-assembly assembly.zip|Successful|
lambda-jobs|lambda|aa-tripplanner-dev-jobs jobs.zip|Successful|
browse-countries|public|GET /api/browse?resource=countries&_cb={cb}|200|(.countries | length) > 0
assembly-coverage|public|GET /api/trip?resource=coverage&trip_id=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|404|.error == "not found"
assembly-itinerary|public|GET /api/trip?trip_id=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|200|.itinerary == [] and .custom_days == []
